{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 14.7% a year from $96.6 billion in FY2017 to $331.8 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F221]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change rather than a cycle: revenue grew 14.3% in FY2018, 6.9% in FY2023, then 15.7% and 17.8% in FY2024 and FY2026 [D46][D311][D364][D472]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 revenue rose $50.1 billion, or 18%, driven by Microsoft Cloud, with Intelligent Cloud led by Azure and Productivity and Business Processes by Microsoft 365 Commercial cloud [P17]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2018 net income fell 35.0% on a 54.6% effective tax rate, which the filing attributes to the net charge from enactment of the TCJA [D48][D32][P61]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Microsoft Cloud supplied 16.2pp of FY2026's 17.8% revenue growth and reached 64.6% of revenue [D568][D472][D566]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Server products and cloud services revenue rose 31% to $129.4 billion, driven by Azure and other cloud services growing 41% [S61][D641][P12]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Intelligent Cloud contributed 11.2pp of FY2026 growth against 6.8pp from Productivity and Business Processes and -0.2pp from More Personal Computing [D917][D892][D942]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 20.8% against revenue growth of 17.8%, an incremental margin of 53.3% [D473][D472][D498]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 7.4% while revenue grew 17.8%, so operating costs grew 10.3pp slower than revenue, at 7.4% [D491][D499]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin reached 46.8% in FY2026, a window high against a 41.7% median and a 30.1% low in FY2017 [F50][D974][D975][D973]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin of 67.9% sat below its 68.2% median and 69.8% FY2024 high, down 0.9pp on cost of revenue [F30][D981][D980][D486]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2026 gross-margin decline came from Intelligent Cloud, where gross margin percentage fell on AI infrastructure investment and sales mix shift to Azure [P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2026 net margin of 40.3% sat 6.5pp below the 46.8% operating margin, as other income of $10.7 billion partly offset a 19.4% tax rate [F70][F50][X124][D458]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $182.9 billion was 1.37x net income, in line with the 1.33x FY2019 level [F100][D459][D86]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow fell 6.5% to $67.0 billion, only 0.50x net income against a 0.91x window median, and its 20.2% margin was the window low [F120][D478][D460][D990][D456][D982]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Capex rose 79.6% to $115.9 billion, 34.9% of revenue and 3.38x D&A, as investing cash use rose on a $51.4 billion increase in property and equipment additions [F110][D479][D455][D461][P1]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow rose $46.8 billion to $182.9 billion on higher cash received from customers and lower income tax payments [P1]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash of $72.9 billion, 22.0% of revenue, ranks in the 83rd percentile of six software peers against a -7.2% median [D465][D466][D1006][D1007]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Total debt fell 6.6% to $40.3 billion while cash and investments rose 2.9% to $113.2 billion [D464][D495][D463][D494]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $22.3 billion plus dividends of $26.4 billion absorbed 72.7% of free cash flow, and the diluted count fell 0.2% [X147][X157][D468][D493]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The current ratio of 1.23x is the window low, but the net cash cushion and $76.8 billion of cash and short-term investments leave liquidity ample [F200][D991][D465][P2]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Free cash flow ran below 80% of net income in FY2025 and FY2026, at 0.70x and 0.50x [R1][D406][D460]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The gap is capex-led rather than earnings-led, so the flag matters as a signal on how long the AI buildout suppresses distributable cash [D460][D455]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2017 pretax income, income tax and receivables were later restated to $29.9 billion, $4.4 billion and $22.4 billion from the first-reported $23.1 billion, $1.9 billion and $19.8 billion [R2][R3][R4][X95][X105][X213]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The FY2017 tax and margin comparisons rest on first-reported values, so the FY2018 tax spike should be read as directionally, not precisely, comparable [R3][D32]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether free cash flow margin recovers above the 30.3% window median from 20.2% in FY2026, reported in the FY2027 10-K cash flow statement [D984][D456]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether capex stays above the 34.9% of revenue reached in FY2026 or falls back toward the 22.9% FY2025 level, disclosed in the FY2027 10-K investing section [D455][D401]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the 41.7% window median after the 46.8% FY2026 high, shown in the FY2027 10-K segment discussion [D975][F50]."}
  ]}
]}
